    <view name="all" class="" db="arabidopsis_NIE_pseudobulk" img="svg_template.svg">
        <webservice>//bar.utoronto.ca/eplant/cgi-bin/plantefp.cgi?datasource=arabidopsis_nat&amp;</webservice>
        <info>
            <li>Single-nucleus RNA-seq profiling of 144,494 Arabidopsis thaliana leaf nuclei across four drought/recovery conditions: well-watered (W0), moderate drought (D0), 15 min after rehydration (R15), and 15 min after watering well-watered plants (W15).</li>
            <li>Plants were grown under long-day conditions (16/8 hour light/dark) at 22°C.</li>
            <li>Moderate drought was applied by withholding water until soil water content reached ~30% of field capacity.</li>
            <li>Nuclei were isolated from fully expanded rosette leaves and profiled using 10x Genomics Chromium single-nucleus RNA-seq (snRNA-seq).</li>
            <li>Cell types identified: Guard, Mesophyll, Epidermal, Trichome, Vascular, Phloem Parenchyma, and Phloem Companion cells.</li>
            <li>Average expression per cell type per condition is displayed (pseudo-bulk, log-normalized counts).</li>
            <li>Results from Illouz-Eliaz et al. (2025) Nature Communications 16: 8095. DOI: 10.1038/s41467-025-63467-2</li>
        </info>

